WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.800
Hello, my name is Kayode Ewumi.
I am an actor and writer,

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.160
and here are five ways to help
you demolish creative blocks.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.680
A creative block is when you're
either creating something,

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.000
making something, and your mind
has totally switched off.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.960
You feel like any time you go
and write that song, that script,

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.000
you go and make something,
you hit a brick wall.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.440
Have you experienced that?

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.960
What I would suggest,
and what helps me,

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:41.000
is getting a blank sheet of paper,
some colouring pencils, pens,

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.760
and just start to sketch
on the piece of paper.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.720
Just sketch, and set a timer
for two minutes.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.200
Then five minutes.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.600
Then 10 minutes.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:50.960
Why?

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:54.160
Why? Because, as kids,
this is what we used to do.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:59.960
And as kids we had this element
of play, of fun, of imagination.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:05.880
Colouring down helps you get any
energy, any stress, any bad vibes,

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.360
on that sheet of paper.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:10.000
The paper will then tell
you how you're feeling.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:13.120
Draw down whatever you want,
however you want.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.640
After that, then try again.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.840
Try and make that thing again,
try and create again.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.320
And you'll see, there'll be a change.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.320
When you read, watch and listen,

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.560
why don't you read something
you haven't read before?

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:32.760
Watch a film you
wouldn't normally watch.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:35.440
A different genre
or from a different era.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.200
Listen to songs you
would never listen to.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.680
Listen to songs with no words.

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:45.880
Listen to rock, rap, hip-hop,
jazz, contemporary.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:50.920
Try and see things, hear things that
you've never heard or seen before.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:55.480
It will help you and will open your
mind to a whole different world.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.280
So, this is what you should do:

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.320
get a notepad, or something
you can write notes in,

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:09.600
jump on any random train,
or random bus,

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.640
and take it to the last stop.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.880
As you're taking this bus or this
train, write down what's around you.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:20.840
Write down what you see or, in fact,
that idea might just come to you.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.440
And make sure you get it down.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.000
Because now's the time.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.080
Normally, if you're in the same
environment, the same room,

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:30.000
the same place,
you see the same things all the time.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.720
And there's no room for inspiration.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.520
So get out of there.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.000
Get out of your room,
get out of your house,

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.600
and let the world
take you on a journey.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.920
Learning an instrument
requires diligence,

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.680
patience and concentration.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:55.080
For me, for example, I started to
learn an instrument at the age of 22.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:58.160
I'm now 25 and no, I'm not the best.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:01.920
But any time I'm writing a script
or trying to create something,

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.000
and I can't do it, I go away
and I play the keyboard for a bit.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.520
Or I go on YouTube and I look
at how to play chords on a guitar.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:11.840
Why?

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.400
Because, for example,
with the guitar,

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.520
unless you get the right chord,

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:19.720
you will not hear that sound,
and that's the same with writing.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:21.720
Unless you get the right thing,

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.960
the right characters,
it will not be what it needs to be.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.160
So instruments teach you diligence,
how to keep on going,

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.040
and keep on going
till you get what's right.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.280
So learn an instrument.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:36.760
I'll say the guitar, it's nice.
It hurts your fingers though, but
hey.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.320
The vomit draft is always
the first draft.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:49.080
And it looks terrible,
it smells horrible.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:52.840
But this is what you need
to begin your journey.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:57.080
If you don't get it down
and it stays here, it's not helpful.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:03:59.680
You don't have to show anybody,

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:04.280
just keep it to yourself, but
make sure you get this draft down.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.320
Forget about what people think.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.400
Forget about what
your mind is telling you.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:09.680
And just do what's right.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:12.200
Get it down and begin your journey.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.300
Thanks for watching.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:20.400
Don't forget to subscribe and click the bell to receive notifications for new videos.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.900
See you again soon!

